# Deploy mobile PHP after every change

PManager’s API is PHP on the live host. After any PHP edit, upload it in the same turn. Do not leave local-only PHP.

## Target (only this folder)

- Local source: `/Users/kangogojoel/StudioProjects/3modernsystems-server/threepmobileserver-src/`
- Remote: `root@212.71.251.143:/var/www/html/threepmobileserver/`
- SSH port: **38000** (not 22)
- App URL: `http://3modernsystems.co.ke/threepmobileserver/`

## Never

- Never overwrite `db.php`
- Never edit or upload `/var/www/html/threepmanager/` (web Ext JS)
- Never commit `db.php` or SSH/DB passwords

## Upload command

```bash
export SSHPASS='<server pass from user>'
RSH='sshpass -e ssh -p 38000 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -o PreferredAuthentications=password -o PubkeyAuthentication=no'
rsync -avz --no-owner --no-group -e "$RSH" \
  --exclude 'db.php' --exclude '3PM.apk' --exclude '*.apk' \
  /Users/kangogojoel/StudioProjects/3modernsystems-server/threepmobileserver-src/ \
  root@212.71.251.143:/var/www/html/threepmobileserver/
```

If Auto-review blocks a password rsync, retry with approval. Confirm remotely with `ls -l` on the uploaded files and that `db.php` mtime is unchanged.

If PHP was changed in this session and not uploaded, upload before finishing.
